  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Isaiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 13,
    "summary": "The destruction of Babylon is a type of the destruction at the Second Coming—It will be a day of wrath and vengeance—Babylon (the world) will fall forever—Compare 2 Nephi 23.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The burden of Babylon, which Isaiah the son of Amoz did see.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "2 Ne. 23:1 (1–22)."
          },
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "“Burden” as used in Isaiah is a message of doom “lifted up” against a people. Isa. 14:28."
          },
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "The historic destruction of wicked Babylon, prophesied in Isa. 13 and 14, is made typical of the ultimate destruction of the whole wicked world. D&C 133:14 (5, 7, 14)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Lift ye up a banner upon the high mountain, exalt the voice unto them, shake the hand, that they may go into the gates of the nobles.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "OR ensign. TG Ensign."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Isa. 2:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "HEB raise."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have commanded my sanctified ones, I have also called my mighty ones for mine anger, even them that rejoice in my highness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "“Sanctified ones” and “saints” are synonymously translated from either of two Hebrew words in the Old Testament."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "Joel 3:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 91
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The noise of a multitude in the mountains, like as of a great people; a tumultuous noise of the kingdoms of nations gathered together: the Lord of hosts mustereth the host of the battle.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "Zeph. 3:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 179,
            "end": 185,
            "text": "TG War."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They come from a far country, from the end of heaven, even the Lord, and the weapons of his indignation, to destroy the whole land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 115,
            "text": "Zech. 12:9 (4, 8–9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Howl ye; for the day of the Lord is at hand; it shall come as a destruction from the Almighty.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "Isa. 14:31."
          },
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Day of the Lord."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore shall all hands be faint, and every man’s heart shall melt:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "Moses 7:66."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And they shall be afraid: pangs and sorrows shall take hold of them; they shall be in pain as a woman that travaileth: they shall be amazed one at another; their faces shall be as flames.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "TG Pain."
          },
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "Hosea 13:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 168,
            "end": 179
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, the day of the Lord cometh, cruel both with wrath and fierce anger, to lay the land desolate: and he shall destroy the sinners thereof out of it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 115,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "TG Earth, Cleansing of; World, End of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the stars of heaven and the constellations thereof shall not give their light: the sun shall be darkened in his going forth, and the moon shall not cause her light to shine.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "Ezek. 32:7 (7–8); Joel 2:10; Matt. 24:29."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And I will punish the world for their evil, and the wicked for their iniquity; and I will cause the arrogancy of the proud to cease, and will lay low the haughtiness of the terrible.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Punish."
          },
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "TG World."
          },
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 165,
            "text": "TG Haughtiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 173,
            "end": 181,
            "text": "HEB tyrants."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 37
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I will make a man more precious than fine gold; even a man than the golden wedge of Ophir.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Isa. 24:6. TG Worth of Souls."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "Job 28:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore I will shake the heavens, and the earth shall remove out of her place, in the wrath of the Lord of hosts, and in the day of his fierce anger.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Hag. 2:6; 2 Ne. 8:6; 3 Ne. 26:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "Isa. 14:26 (22–26); 24:1; D&C 88:87 (87–92)."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Earth, Renewal of."
          },
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 150,
            "text": "Lam. 1:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And it shall be as the chased roe, and as a sheep that no man taketh up: they shall every man turn to his own people, and flee every one into his own land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "OR hunted deer."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "HEB none gathers in."
          },
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 116,
            "text": "Jer. 50:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 150,
            "end": 154,
            "text": "TG Lands of Inheritance."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Every one that is found shall be thrust through; and every one that is joined unto them shall fall by the sword.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "OR pierced or stabbed."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Their children also shall be dashed to pieces before their eyes; their houses shall be spoiled, and their wives ravished.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Nahum 3:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Zech. 14:2 (1–2)."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "OR plundered."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, I will stir up the Medes against them, which shall not regard silver; and as for gold, they shall not delight in it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "Dan. 5:30–31."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 88
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Their bows also shall dash the young men to pieces; and they shall have no pity on the fruit of the womb; their eye shall not spare children.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Babylon, the glory of kingdoms, the beauty of the Chaldees’ excellency, shall be as when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "TG Babylon."
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "HEB vainglorious grandeur of the Babylonians."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Isa. 23:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "Jer. 20:16; Amos 4:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "Gen. 19:24; Jer. 50:40."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It shall never be inhabited, neither shall it be dwelt in from generation to generation: neither shall the Arabian pitch tent there; neither shall the shepherds make their fold there.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "Jer. 50:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But wild beasts of the desert shall lie there; and their houses shall be full of doleful creatures; and owls shall dwell there, and satyrs shall dance there.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Isa. 34:14 (11–15)."
          },
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "HEB he-goats, or demons."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the wild beasts of the islands shall cry in their desolate houses, and dragons in their pleasant palaces: and her time is near to come, and her days shall not be prolonged.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "HEB palaces."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "HEB (perhaps) jackals, or wild dogs."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 91
          },
          {
            "start": 123,
            "end": 125
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
